Third-party components and their licences:

- The recipe skeleton (boot.py, benchmarks/, tests/, the Engram row-store idea and
  the Docker layout) originates from 0xSero/deepseek-v4.1-flash-4x-rtx-pro-6000,
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 0xSero. The MIT notice is retained in
  LICENSE.upstream-MIT as that licence requires; the combined work is offered
  under the AGPL-3.0-or-later.
- runtime/flash_mla_sm120.py is derived from SGLang and remains under the Apache
  License 2.0 (LICENSE.sglang); the page-split changes are distributed under the
  same terms.
- runtime/sglang/deepseekv41_detector.py is sgl-project/sglang
  python/sglang/srt/function_call/deepseekv41_detector.py at commit 464fffbec8d0
  (SGLang #39665), unmodified, Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.sglang). The default
  image installs it through runtime/patch_v41_tool_constraint.py.
- patches/nccl-2393-aarch64-cts-fence.patch is Stanislav Bardyuk's change from
  NVIDIA/nccl PR #2393 (commit b85c5d9c4aa5), backported to NCCL v2.30.7-1;
  Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.sglang contains the same Apache-2.0 text).
- runtime/b12x/b12x/comm/roce_ring is the path-aware RoCEnante package of
  FujitsuPolycom/sparkring (commit f16b5f4), itself derived from local-inference-lab/b12x
  (RoCEnante, PR 295); Apache License 2.0 (runtime/b12x/LICENSE). Origin and local
  changes: runtime/b12x/roce_ring-provenance.json. scripts/ring_mesh/plan.py drives
  sparkring's fabric planner and the units run sparkring's RDMA-TX marker; neither is
  vendored here (both come from a sparkring checkout, Apache License 2.0).
- runtime/b12x_next is local-inference-lab/b12x (Luke Alonso and Jason / original-el8)
  at commit a7d7d29b2ef8869086e0ceaa787321f17544e3c9, renamed b12x -> b12x_next by
  scripts/build_b12x_next.sh so it can sit beside runtime/b12x; Apache License 2.0
  (runtime/b12x_next/LICENSE). Local changes are the patches that script applies, in
  order (scripts/b12x_next-*.patch; their combined sha256 prefix is
  runtime/b12x_next/b12x_next/SOURCE_PATCH): compact-n64-m64, prequant-input,
  barrier-zero, det-triton-planner and claim-barrier. claim-barrier is a backport
  of b12x commit d7937d7fc2e5511a0b61eb3572cd149f563f9b4f by Martin Vit (a CTA
  barrier after the dynamic kernel's producer-loop batch-claim read, closing a
  shared-memory reuse race on ctrl[7]); b12x development continues in
  flashinfer-ai/flashinfer (flashinfer/experimental/b12x, Apache License 2.0).
  The changes are distributed under the same licence.
- runtime/b12x/b12x/comm/roce_twoshot is a copy of runtime/b12x/b12x/comm/roce with the
  pipelined two-shot all-reduce of flashinfer-ai/flashinfer PR 6915 by Luke Alonso (head
  effeb496, flashinfer/experimental/b12x/comm/roce, itself local-inference-lab/b12x's
  RoCEnante) ported in; Apache License 2.0 (runtime/b12x/LICENSE). FlashInfer: Copyright
  2025-2026 NVIDIA; Copyright 2023-2026 FlashInfer community (https://flashinfer.ai/).
  Origin and local changes: runtime/b12x/twoshot-provenance.json. It is opt-in
  (DSV41_ROCE_TWOSHOT=1); runtime/b12x/b12x/comm/roce is unchanged.
- runtime/flashinfer_pce/base is an unmodified copy of FlashInfer's SM120 sparse-MLA sources
  (flashinfer 0.6.18, git 69ff11fc, as installed in the DS v2.6 image; NVIDIA, BSD-3-Clause,
  headers retained), kept for
  the offline tests and the approved source closure of runtime/flashinfer_pce/gen_pce_sources.py
  (csrc/tvm_ffi_utils.h and include/flashinfer/layout.cuh are FlashInfer's, Apache License 2.0).
  That generator derives the opt-in DSV41_PREFILL_NATIVE_EXTRA module from the image's own
  FlashInfer sources at build time
  (dual-cache prefill dispatch opened to 128/256-token extra pages, symbols renamed); origin and
  changes: runtime/flashinfer_pce/PROVENANCE.json.
- SGLang, FlashInfer, DeepGEMM, PyTorch, NVIDIA components and the DeepSeek model
  retain their respective upstream licences. This repository does not
  redistribute model weights.
